        heading: "6. Deep Dive Flows (Flow 1 & Flow 2)",
        body: "We examine the two defining mechanisms of a modern cloud drive: (Flow 1) Content-Defined Chunking (Rabin Fingerprinting) + CAS Upload with Deduplication, and (Flow 2) Multi-Device Delta Sync with Optimistic Concurrency Conflict Resolution.",
        bullets: [
          "Flow 1 — Content-Defined Chunking & CAS Deduplication Upload: Why not split files at fixed 4 MB offsets? Because inserting 1 byte at index 0 of a 100 MB file shifts every single 4 MB boundary by 1 byte, invalidating all 25 chunk hashes! Instead, the client slides a 48-byte window across the file computing a Rabin-Karp polynomial rolling hash. Whenever `rollingHash & 0x3FFFFF == 0` (which happens on average every $2^{22} = 4\\text{ MB}$, bounded between `MIN_CHUNK = 2 MB` and `MAX_CHUNK = 8 MB`), it declares a chunk boundary based *purely on local byte content*. Subsequent chunks remain 100% identical and are skipped via the server's CAS precheck.",
          "Flow 2 — Multi-Device Delta Sync & OCC Conflict Resolution: Each workspace maintains a monotonically increasing Log Sequence Number (`latest_lsn`). When Device A commits version 5 of `report.pdf` (based on `expectedBaseVersion = 4`), the database executes an atomic compare-and-swap. If Device B was offline and later tries to commit its own edits also claiming `expectedBaseVersion = 4`, the OCC check sees `currentVersion == 5 != 4`. Instead of overwriting Device A's work or failing silently, the server branches Device B's revision into a new sibling file node `report (Device B's conflicted copy 2026-09-30).pdf` so zero user work is ever lost."
        ],
        codeSnippet: {
          title: "Flow 1 (Rabin Content-Defined Chunker) & Flow 2 (OCC Revision Commit) in Java",
          code: "/*\n================================================================================\nFLOW 1: CONTENT-DEFINED CHUNKING (RABIN ROLLING HASH) + CAS DEDUP UPLOAD\n================================================================================\nOriginal File : [ Chunk 0 (4.1MB) | Chunk 1 (3.8MB) | Chunk 2 (4.5MB) ]\n10KB Edit in 0: [ Chunk 0' (4.11MB)| Chunk 1 (SAME!) | Chunk 2 (SAME!) ]\n1. Client runs Rabin Chunker -> Computes SHA-256 for [Chunk 0', Chunk 1, Chunk 2]\n2. POST /files/revisions/init -> Server checks cas_blocks table:\n   - Chunk 1 & Chunk 2 ALREADY EXIST -> Skipped!\n   - Chunk 0' MISSING -> Server returns Presigned S3 PUT URL for Chunk 0' only.\n3. Client uploads Chunk 0' directly to S3 -> Calls POST /commit.\n\n================================================================================\nFLOW 2: ATOMIC REVISION COMMIT & CONFLICT COPY BRANCHING\n================================================================================\nDevice A & Device B both start at baseVersion = 4.\n1. Device A commits first -> DB CAS (curr_version: 4 -> 5), LSN = 1092.\n2. Device B commits with expectedBaseVersion = 4 -> DB CAS sees curr_version (5) != 4!\n3. Server automatically creates \"report (Conflicted Copy).pdf\" at version 1, LSN = 1093.\n4. SSE Notification pushes LSN 1093 -> Both devices sync both files cleanly.\n*/\n\npackage com.sdi.filestorage.service;\n\nimport com.sdi.filestorage.domain.*;\nimport java.security.MessageDigest;\nimport java.time.Instant;\nimport java.time.LocalDate;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class FileSyncEngine {\n\n    // Rabin-Karp Content-Defined Chunking constants\n    private static final int MIN_CHUNK_SIZE = 2 * 1024 * 1024; // 2 MB\n    private static final int MAX_CHUNK_SIZE = 8 * 1024 * 1024; // 8 MB\n    private static final long AVG_CHUNK_MASK = (1L << 22) - 1; // 4 MB average cut-point\n\n    /**\n     * FLOW 1 (Client-Side SDK): Content-Defined Chunking via Rolling Hash\n     */\n    public List<BlockDescriptor> splitFileContentDefined(byte[] fileBytes) throws Exception {\n        List<BlockDescriptor> blocks = new ArrayList<>();\n        int chunkStart = 0;\n        long rollingHash = 0;\n        int blockIndex = 0;\n\n        for (int i = 0; i < fileBytes.length; i++) {\n            rollingHash = (rollingHash * 31 + (fileBytes[i] & 0xFF));\n            int currentChunkLen = i - chunkStart + 1;\n\n            boolean isCutPoint = (currentChunkLen >= MIN_CHUNK_SIZE && (rollingHash & AVG_CHUNK_MASK) == 0)\n                              || (currentChunkLen >= MAX_CHUNK_SIZE)\n                              || (i == fileBytes.length - 1);\n\n            if (isCutPoint) {\n                MessageDigest digest = MessageDigest.getInstance(\"SHA-256\");\n                digest.update(fileBytes, chunkStart, currentChunkLen);\n                String sha256Hex = HexFormat.of().formatHex(digest.digest());\n\n                blocks.add(new BlockDescriptor(blockIndex++, sha256Hex, currentChunkLen));\n                chunkStart = i + 1;\n                rollingHash = 0;\n            }\n        }\n        return blocks;\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * FLOW 2 (Server-Side): Atomic OCC Revision Commit with Automatic Conflict Copy Forking\n     */\n    public WorkspaceDeltaEvent commitRevisionTransactional(\n        MetadataRepository repo,\n        NotificationBus notificationBus,\n        UUID workspaceId,\n        UUID fileId,\n        int expectedBaseVersion,\n        List<BlockDescriptor> blocks,\n        long userId\n    ) {\n        return repo.executeInTransaction(tx -> {\n            // 1. Verify all referenced CAS blocks are uploaded & VERIFIED in S3\n            Set<String> hashes = new HashSet<>();\n            blocks.forEach(b -> hashes.add(b.sha256Hash()));\n            if (!tx.allBlocksVerified(hashes)) {\n                throw new IllegalStateException(\"Cannot commit revision: missing unverified CAS blocks\");\n            }\n\n            FileNodeEntity currentFile = tx.lockFileForUpdate(fileId);\n            long nextLsn = tx.incrementWorkspaceLsn(workspaceId);\n\n            // 2. Check Optimistic Concurrency Control (expectedBaseVersion == currentVersion)\n            if (currentFile.currentVersion() == expectedBaseVersion) {\n                int newVersion = currentFile.currentVersion() + 1;\n                tx.updateFileVersion(fileId, newVersion);\n                tx.insertFileRevision(fileId, newVersion, nextLsn, blocks, userId);\n                tx.incrementBlockRefCounts(hashes);\n\n                WorkspaceDeltaEvent event = new WorkspaceDeltaEvent(\n                    nextLsn, fileId, currentFile.fileName(), newVersion, false, blocks, Instant.now()\n                );\n                tx.appendWorkspaceJournal(workspaceId, event);\n                notificationBus.publishWorkspaceLsn(workspaceId, nextLsn);\n                return event;\n            } else {\n                // 3. Conflict detected! Fork into a deterministic \"Conflicted Copy\" file node\n                UUID conflictFileId = UUID.randomUUID();\n                String conflictName = buildConflictFileName(currentFile.fileName(), userId);\n\n                tx.createFileNode(conflictFileId, workspaceId, currentFile.parentFolderId(), conflictName);\n                tx.insertFileRevision(conflictFileId, 1, nextLsn, blocks, userId);\n                tx.incrementBlockRefCounts(hashes);\n\n                WorkspaceDeltaEvent conflictEvent = new WorkspaceDeltaEvent(\n                    nextLsn, conflictFileId, conflictName, 1, false, blocks, Instant.now()\n                );\n                tx.appendWorkspaceJournal(workspaceId, conflictEvent);\n                notificationBus.publishWorkspaceLsn(workspaceId, nextLsn);\n                return conflictEvent;\n            }\n        });\n    }\n\n    private String buildConflictFileName(String originalName, long userId) {\n        int dotIdx = originalName.lastIndexOf('.');\n        String suffix = \" (Conflicted copy \" + LocalDate.now() + \" by user-\" + userId + \")\";\n        return (dotIdx == -1)\n            ? originalName + suffix\n            : originalName.substring(0, dotIdx) + suffix + originalName.substring(dotIdx);\n    }\n}"
        }
