        heading: "6. Deep Dive Flows (Flow 1 & Flow 2)",
        body: "Below we trace (Flow 1) Two-Phase Atomic Multi-Seat Hold with Lazy Expiration and OCC, and (Flow 2) Virtual Waiting Room Queue Admission & Contiguous 'Best Available' Seat Allocation.",
        bullets: [
          "Flow 1 — Atomic Multi-Seat Hold with Lazy Expiration & OCC: Suppose 1,000 users click seats `[101, 102]` at the exact same millisecond. First, a Redis Lua script checks if `seat:101` and `seat:102` are currently held; 999 requests fail in <0.5ms at the Redis layer without ever touching PostgreSQL. The 1 winning request proceeds to PostgreSQL, sorts the seat IDs `[101, 102]`, and executes an atomic update that succeeds *either* if `status = 'AVAILABLE'` *or* if `status = 'HELD' AND hold_expires_at < NOW()` (Lazy Expiration!). This means even if a background cron job is delayed by 30 seconds, an expired seat hold is immediately bookable the exact millisecond `hold_expires_at` passes.",
          "Flow 2 — Virtual Waiting Room & 'Best Available' Bitmask Search: For mega-events, showing a clickable 80,000-seat map causes severe contention because thousands of fans click the exact same front-row seats. Instead, the UI switches to 'Section / Best Available' mode: the user asks for `N = 4` contiguous seats in `Section 102`. The Booking Service represents each row of 32 seats as a 32-bit integer bitmask in memory (`0` = available, `1` = taken) and finds `N` adjacent available seats in $O(1)$ CPU cycles using bitwise shifts (`mask & (mask << 1) & (mask << 2) & (mask << 3)`)."
        ],
        codeSnippet: {
          title: "Flow 1 (Atomic Multi-Seat Hold with Lazy Expiration OCC) & Flow 2 (Bitwise Contiguous Seat Finder) in Java",
          code: "/*\n================================================================================\nFLOW 1: TWO-PHASE ATOMIC MULTI-SEAT HOLD (REDIS GATE + DB OCC WITH LAZY EXPIRY)\n================================================================================\n1. Sort requested seatIds ascending: [102, 101] -> [101, 102] (Prevents Deadlock)\n2. Redis Lua Gatekeeper: All-or-nothing SETNX on hold:{showId}:{seatId} (EX 600s)\n   -> 999 of 1,000 concurrent callers fast-fail here in 0.4ms!\n3. PostgreSQL Authoritative OCC Update:\n   UPDATE show_seats\n   SET status = 'HELD', held_by_user = :userId, booking_id = :bookingId,\n       hold_expires_at = NOW() + INTERVAL '10 minutes', version = version + 1\n   WHERE show_id = :showId AND seat_id IN (101, 102)\n     AND (status = 'AVAILABLE' OR (status = 'HELD' AND hold_expires_at < NOW()));\n   -> Assert updatedRows == seatIds.size() (else ROLLBACK & release Redis keys)\n\n================================================================================\nFLOW 2: CONTIGUOUS SEAT ALLOCATION VIA BITMASK (\"BEST AVAILABLE\" MODE)\n================================================================================\nRow A (16 seats): 1 = Available, 0 = Taken/Held\nBitmask: 0b00111100_11001110  -> Looking for k=4 contiguous seats -> Match at bits 10..13!\n*/\n\npackage com.sdi.ticketbooking.service;\n\nimport com.sdi.ticketbooking.domain.*;\nimport java.time.Duration;\nimport java.time.Instant;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class SeatReservationEngine {\n\n    private static final Duration HOLD_TTL = Duration.ofMinutes(10);\n\n    private final RedisSeatLockClient redisLockClient;\n    private final SeatDatabaseRepository seatRepo;\n\n    public SeatReservationEngine(RedisSeatLockClient redisLockClient, SeatDatabaseRepository seatRepo) {\n        this.redisLockClient = redisLockClient;\n        this.seatRepo = seatRepo;\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * FLOW 1: Two-Phase Atomic Seat Hold with Deadlock Avoidance & Lazy Expiration\n     */\n    public HoldSeatsResponse holdSeatsAtomically(long userId, long showId, List<Long> rawSeatIds) {\n        if (rawSeatIds == null || rawSeatIds.isEmpty() || rawSeatIds.size() > 6) {\n            throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"Must select between 1 and 6 seats\");\n        }\n\n        // 1. Sort seat IDs ascending to guarantee deadlock-free lock acquisition order\n        List<Long> sortedSeatIds = rawSeatIds.stream().distinct().sorted().toList();\n        UUID bookingId = UUID.randomUUID();\n        Instant expiresAt = Instant.now().plus(HOLD_TTL);\n\n        // 2. Fast-Fail Redis Lua Gatekeeper (Atomic All-or-Nothing SETNX with 600s TTL)\n        boolean redisLocked = redisLockClient.tryAcquireMultiSeatHold(\n            showId, sortedSeatIds, bookingId.toString(), (int) HOLD_TTL.toSeconds()\n        );\n        if (!redisLocked) {\n            throw new SeatUnavailableException(\"One or more selected seats are currently held\");\n        }\n\n        try {\n            // 3. Authoritative ACID Database Transaction with Lazy Expiration Check\n            return seatRepo.executeInTransaction(tx -> {\n                Instant now = Instant.now();\n                int updatedCount = tx.claimAvailableOrExpiredSeats(\n                    showId, sortedSeatIds, userId, bookingId, now, expiresAt\n                );\n\n                // All-or-nothing check: if any seat was already BOOKED or actively HELD, abort!\n                if (updatedCount != sortedSeatIds.size()) {\n                    throw new SeatUnavailableException(\"Seat state changed concurrently; aborting hold\");\n                }\n\n                long totalCents = tx.calculateTotalPriceCents(showId, sortedSeatIds);\n                tx.insertPendingBooking(bookingId, userId, showId, totalCents, expiresAt);\n\n                return new HoldSeatsResponse(\n                    bookingId, showId, sortedSeatIds, totalCents, expiresAt, \"pay_tok_\" + bookingId\n                );\n            });\n        } catch (Exception ex) {\n            // Compensating action: immediately free the Redis hold keys so others can book\n            redisLockClient.releaseMultiSeatHold(showId, sortedSeatIds, bookingId.toString());\n            throw ex;\n        }\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * FLOW 2: O(1) Bitwise Finder for K Contiguous Available Seats in a Row\n     * @param availabilityBitmask 64-bit mask where 1 = AVAILABLE, 0 = HELD/BOOKED\n     * @param k number of adjacent seats requested (e.g., 4)\n     * @return starting seat index (0-based), or -1 if no k contiguous seats exist in this row\n     */\n    public int findContiguousSeatsBitwise(long availabilityBitmask, int k) {\n        long mask = availabilityBitmask;\n        for (int shift = 1; shift < k; shift++) {\n            mask &= (availabilityBitmask >>> shift);\n        }\n        if (mask == 0L) {\n            return -1; // No k adjacent available seats in this row\n        }\n        // Return the lowest-numbered contiguous block using trailing zeros\n        return Long.numberOfTrailingZeros(mask);\n    }\n}"
        }
